    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302-a1">

                <pb facs="0378" n="280" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg280"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Memorandum.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Cablegram from Liu Kun-Yi, viceroy at
                        Nankin, dated July 21, 1900, and received by Minister Wu at 10 a.m. the same
                        day. Left at the Department of State July 21, 1900.</hi></p>
                <p>According to edict of 22d of this (sixth) moon (July 18), with the exception of
                    the German minister who was killed by anarchists, with regard to which rigorous
                    measures are being taken to investigate and punish the guilty parties, all the
                    other ministers, to whom strenuous efforts are being made to afford protection,
                    are fortunately unharmed.</p>
            </div>
